<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Queen Victoria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1819">1819</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Victoria of the United Kingdom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victoria was queen of the United Kingdom from 1837 to 1901 and empress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1876. Her long reign saw industrial growth, political reform and the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>. Her mother was a princess of Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a> whose first marriage had been to a prince of Leiningen. She chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a> as the capital of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/queen-victoria.jpg" alt="Queen Victoria" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Bassano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Victoria_by_Bassano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
